---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Downloads"
  description="Find the maintained Atrinik Classic releases and learn the status of the next-generation replacement stack."
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Choose your path</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">Play the classic. Follow what comes next.</h1>
    <p class="page-lede">
      Atrinik Classic is the current playable game. The next-generation stack
      remains in development and does not have a public download yet.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="download-paths-heading">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Release status</p>
      <h2 id="download-paths-heading">Two lines, clearly labeled</h2>
      <p>
        Classic and next-generation software have different licenses and
        different levels of readiness.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="split-grid">
      <article class="path-card path-card--classic">
        <div class="path-card-topline">
          <span class="path-number">Path I</span>
          <span class="status-tag status-tag--live">Playable now</span>
        </div>
        <h3>Atrinik Classic</h3>
        <p>
          The maintained GPL-2.0-or-later line is the way to play Atrinik today.
          Use its GitHub Releases page and read the notes for the available
          packages, platforms, and compatibility details.
        </p>
        <ul class="path-details">
          <li>Current playable implementation</li>
          <li>Maintained releases</li>
          <li>GPL-2.0-or-later software</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="card-actions">
          <a
            class="button button--primary"
            href="https://github.com/atrinik/classic/releases"
            >View Classic releases</a
          >
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="path-card path-card--future">
        <div class="path-card-topline">
          <span class="path-number">Path II</span>
          <span class="status-tag">Not yet downloadable</span>
        </div>
        <h3>Next generation</h3>
        <p>
          The clean-room MIT-licensed Go and Rust replacement stack is still in
          development. No next-generation build is being offered for download
          here.
        </p>
        <ul class="path-details">
          <li>Clean-room Go and Rust stack</li>
          <li>MIT-licensed software</li>
          <li>No public download</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="card-actions">
          <a
            class="link-arrow"
            href="https://github.com/atrinik/atrinik/issues/168"
          >
            Follow the replacement roadmap <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="catalog-heading">
    <aside class="callout">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">An honest download boundary</p>
        <h2 id="catalog-heading">No site-verified immutable catalog yet</h2>
        <p>
          This site does not yet have a verified catalog of exact versions,
          checksums, platforms, compatibility, provenance, and licenses. Until
          that exists, it links to the owning repository’s release page instead
          of guessing direct artifact URLs.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card-actions">
        <a class="button button--ghost" href="/licenses/"
          >Understand the licenses</a
        >
      </div>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="before-heading">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Before you begin</p>
      <h2 id="before-heading">Check the release that you choose</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="detail-grid">
      <article class="detail-card">
        <h3>Read the release notes</h3>
        <p>
          Confirm the supported platform and any compatibility guidance on the
          Classic release page before installing a package.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="detail-card">
        <h3>Keep licenses distinct</h3>
        <p>
          Classic software is GPL-2.0-or-later. Maps, graphics, audio, and other
          authored content can carry separate, per-file terms.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="detail-card">
        <h3>Watch the roadmap</h3>
        <p>
          Next-generation availability will be announced through the project’s
          public development and release process when it is ready.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
